       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the usual maximum dose of 10 mg daily. Higher doses mostly add peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If you're intentionally going above the labeled maximum, tell me and I'll enter it. I'd add a note such as \"dose exceeds labeled max, confirmed with attending\".\n3. **A different dose or regimen.** For example, 10 mg of amlodipine plus a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic. A typo for 2.5 mg or 5 mg is also possible."
